  "note": "Triennial election of the councillors of Londonderry Corporation, polled Wednesday 18 May 1949 (the aldermanships were not included). The Unionist nominees for the North Ward were returned unopposed on nomination day, 4 May (Derry Journal, 6 May 1949, p. 5); the Irish Labour Party contested the South and Waterside wards. Result: Anti-Partitionists 7 seats instead of 4; Unionist control retained. All six were retiring councillors; the label is the Journal's description, not a per-name label. Returned unopposed."
